Australian Curriculum attribution
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Senior secondary curriculum descriptors in this package are derived from the
Australian Curriculum (Senior Secondary Version 8.4). F-10 (Version 9.0)
skills use ACARA codes as tags; their names and descriptions are this
project's own wording (see "Which files carry ACARA text" below).

(c) Australian Curriculum, Assessment and Reporting Authority (ACARA) 2010 to
present, unless otherwise indicated. This material was downloaded from the
Australian Curriculum website (https://www.australiancurriculum.edu.au)
(accessed 8 September 2026) and was modified. The four senior secondary
mathematics subject pages (Version 8.4) were downloaded from the archived
Version 8 site, https://v8.australiancurriculum.edu.au (accessed 8 September
2026). The senior secondary skill names and descriptions derived from ACARA
descriptors were changed as follows:

  - most names have the initial letter capitalised and the final full stop
    dropped;
  - curly quotation marks are straightened;
  - where a descriptor has several clauses or examples, the name is shortened
    (some names stop part-way through the descriptor);
  - mathematical notation is simplified to plain text, for example
    \(x^2\) becomes x^2 and \(\frac{a}{b}\) becomes a/b; some names still
    keep the original LaTeX notation;
  - some names are reworded in this project's own words, keeping the topic
    of the descriptor; a few carry small transcription slips (punctuation,
    stray spacing, a dropped letter or a dropped word);
  - in many descriptions the descriptor, lower-cased, is embedded in a
    template sentence ("Given bounded, fully specified inputs, ...");
    other descriptions are this project's own wording.

