Which files carry ACARA text:

  - Skill files for the senior secondary curriculum (ids starting
    "senior-"): the name, and in many files the description, are modified
    ACARA descriptors as described above. Each of these files starts with a
    comment saying so. The ids and file names of these skills are lowercase
    slugs of the (shortened) descriptor, and some carry a tag that is a short
    hyphenated phrase from it.
  - Code comments, docstrings and tests: many quote ACARA descriptor words
    (Version 8.4, and in a few places Version 9.0), for example to say which
    descriptor a generator or test is for. Quotes may be shortened or
    re-cased. The quoted words are ACARA's, remain under CC BY 4.0 on ACARA's
    terms, and are credited by this NOTICE.
  - Codes: ACARA content description codes (for example ACMSM104 and
    AC9M2N03) appear as tags, in lower case or upper case (acmsm104,
    ac9m2n03, ACMSM072).
    Codes also appear in the ids and descriptions of some senior secondary
    skills, and in code comments and tests. A code is an identifier, not
    curriculum text.
  - F-10 skills (ids starting "f10-" and a few others tagged acara-f10-v9):
    names and descriptions are this project's own wording. They may share
    ordinary phrases with the curriculum (for example "Represent and order
    numbers to 120"), and carry ACARA codes in tags only.

Everything else in this package, including generated questions, answers,
distractors, misconceptions, skill structure and mappings, is the project's
own work and is not ACARA material.

